  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_spikenard_cb1e4e83ca23ca753430bcb24fb57b0b4d388eecc1b36296c479c9f14dc551e69d9">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>spikenard, an aromatic substance from a plant (Nardostachys Jatamansi) growing in India (Pegolotti 430; OED s.v. spikenard; MED s.v. spikenard n.); also called spica celtica, spica seltica (see also spyknard); used medicinally in herbal remedies; the meaning of arote (in spignarde arote) is unknown</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
